# Batch-Live Symmetry: 90% Shared

RULE: Services MUST support `--mode batch|live` with a shared engine. Only 4 seams differ between modes.
WHY: Eliminates code drift between backtest and production; changes to logic apply to both modes automatically.
CODEX: 04-architecture/batch-live-symmetry.md

The 4 mode-specific seams:
  1. Data source   — batch: GCS historical; live: WebSocket/REST stream
  2. Data sink     — batch: GCS write; live: Pub/Sub publish
  3. Persistence   — batch: no thread; live: background persistence thread
  4. Trigger       — batch: date range loop; live: event-driven callback

The shared engine (90%):
  Business logic, feature calculation, validation, schema, event logging,
  error handling, config loading, instrument resolution — ALL mode-agnostic.

DO:
  class MyEngine:  # mode-agnostic, receives data via injected adapter
      def process(self, record: MySchema) -> None: ...

NEVER:
  if mode == "batch": ... else: ...  # inside engine logic
  Duplicate business logic between batch and live paths
  Mode-specific imports at engine level
